content.thinking:
Wait, there's still the problem that the todos are saved before route() is called. When init() is called, it loads the filter, then applies the hash. On a new window the hash is empty, so it keeps the stored filter. Then route() reads the hash again (still empty) and applies... actually `applyHashFilter()` doesn't change the filter if the hash is empty. Then when route() is called separately, it reads the hash again and if it's empty, sets filter to 'all'. Wait, the route() method now does:

```
route() {
  const hash = win.location.hash || '#/';
  if (hash === '#/active') this.filter = 'active';
  else if (hash === '#/completed') this.filter = 'completed';
  else this.filter = 'all';
  this.saveFilter();
  this.render();
}
```

So route() will set filter to 'all' because hash is empty. This overrides the stored filter. I shouldn't call route() after init. Let me just call init() which already handles the filter correctly.

